{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_f9fcfb86-6d5f-4879-9623-ebada846de40","role":"user","created":1789882998,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"call_5935b064b12a47b88c08a5a9","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"resultType":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","text":"package cards\n\n// static_unmapped:skip_next_untap round (ticket #3458, REPARSE-MAP demand:\n// \"It doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.\" — Chill of\n// the Grave, Crippling Chill, Ojutai's Breath, Press for Answers class).\n//\n// Reuses Card.SkipNextUntap (card.go, Exert) and its sole consumer\n// Zone.UntapAll (zone.go) completely unchanged — that field/consumer pair\n// already implements \"this permanent skips its controller's next untap\n// step, then the flag clears,\" one permanent at a time, exactly this\n// family's semantics. Only a new effect name was missing to SET the field\n// from a targeted spell/ability effect (the field was previously only ever\n// set by Exert's own hand-authored code path). Fixed by adding `case\n// \"skip_next_untap_step\"` (game/ability_effects.go), mirroring\n// tap_target_creatures/untap_target_permanent's per-target\n// battlefield-lookup shape.\n\nfunc init() {\n\tregEffect(\"skip_next_untap_step\", Primitive{\n\t\tExecutor:  \"game/ability_effects.go case \\\"skip_next_untap_step\\\" -> loops stackObj.Targets, gs.Battlefield.GetCard(target.CardID), sets Card.SkipNextUntap = true (consumed one-shot by Zone.UntapAll, same field Exert uses); shared by triggered/activated ability effects AND v2 spell-effect-sequence atoms (same chokepoint as \\\"tap_target_creatures\\\"/\\\"untap_target_permanent\\\")\",\n\t\tShapeTest: \"TestSkipNextUntapStep_TargetDoesntUntapNextStep (game/skip_next_untap_step_target_test.go)\",\n\t})\n}\n=== 13cd0f106c ===\npackage cards\n\n// verb_unmapped:tap round (ticket engine.auto-prevent-untap-until-next-\n// untap, REPARSE-MAP demand: \"tap that creature and it doesn't untap\n// during its controller's next untap step\" -- Kashi-Tribe Reaver class).\n//\n// The referent (\"that creature\") is the same triggered ability's own\n// target, already resolved into stackObj.Targets by the time the effect\n// atom resolves. A plain \"tap\"/\"tap_target\" mapping silently drops the\n// follow-up clause, and the existing bare prevent-untap atoms\n// (skip_next_untap_step, referent_doesnt_untap_next_step) drop the tap,\n// so the shape needs a single PAIRED atom. Fixed by adding `case\n// \"tap_referent_doesnt_untap\"` (game/ability_effects.go), which taps each\n// supplied target with full card.Tap() + EventTapped/EventBecomesTapped\n// semantics AND sets Card.SkipNextUntap -- the existing exert-mechanic\n// flag (Rule 701.39) consumed one-shot by Zone.UntapAll, so the effect is\n// duration-bounded to the controller's next untap step and self-clears.\n//\n// Scope: only the referent/paired form. A bare \"Tap target creature\" (no\n// follow-up clause) stays a plain \"tap\" with no prevent-untap side\n// effect; a bare \"Untap target permanent\" is untouched.\n\nfunc init() {\n\tregEffect(\"tap_referent_doesnt_untap\", Primitive{\n\t\tExecutor:  \"game/ability_effects.go case \\\"tap_referent_doesnt_untap\\\" -> loops stackObj.Targets, gs.Battlefield.GetCard(target.CardID), card.Tap() + EventTapped/EventBecomesTapped AND sets Card.SkipNextUntap = true (consumed one-shot by Zone.UntapAll, same field Exert uses); paired tap+prevent-untap atom shared by triggered/activated ability effects AND v2 spell-effect-sequence atoms\",\n\t\tShapeTest: \"TestTapReferentDoesntUntap_TapsAndSkipsControllersNextUntapStep (game/factory_ng_13cd0f106c_test.go)\",\n\t})\n}\n=== 565337de28 ===\npackage cards\n\n// no_untap_next_step primitive (ticket engine.auto-no-untap-next-step-\n// 565337de28, Quiet Contemplation class): \"tap target creature an\n// opponent controls and it doesn't untap during its controller's next\n// untap step.\" Mirrors tap_referent_doesnt_untap's paired tap+prevent-\n// untap shape (game/registry_factory_ng_13cd0f106c.go) under its own\n// effect name.\n\nfunc init() {\n\tregEffect(\"no_untap_next_step\", Primitive{\n\t\tExecutor:  \"game/ability_effects.go case \\\"no_untap_next_step\\\" -> loops stackObj.Targets, gs.Battlefield.GetCard(target.CardID), card.Tap() + EventTapped/EventBecomesTapped AND sets Card.SkipNextUntap = true (consumed one-shot by Zone.UntapAll, same field Exert uses); paired tap+prevent-untap atom for the Quiet Contemplation oracle family\",\n\t\tShapeTest: \"TestFactoryNGNoUntapNextStep (game/factory_ng_565337de28_test.go)\",\n\t})\n}","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"package cards\n\n// static_unmapped:skip_next_untap round (ticket #3458, REPARSE-MAP demand:\n// \"It doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.\" — Chill of\n// the Grave, Crippling Chill, Ojutai's Breath, Press for Answers class).\n//\n// Reuses Card.SkipNextUntap (card.go, Exert) and its sole consumer\n// Zone.UntapAll (zone.go) completely unchanged — that field/consumer pair\n// already implements \"this permanent skips its controller's next untap\n// step, then the flag clears,\" one permanent at a time, exactly this\n// family's semantics. Only a new effect name was missing to SET the field\n// from a targeted spell/ability effect (the field was previously only ever\n// set by Exert's own hand-authored code path). Fixed by adding `case\n// \"skip_next_untap_step\"` (game/ability_effects.go), mirroring\n// tap_target_creatures/untap_target_permanent's per-target\n// battlefield-lookup shape.\n\nfunc init() {\n\tregEffect(\"skip_next_untap_step\", Primitive{\n\t\tExecutor:  \"game/ability_effects.go case \\\"skip_next_untap_step\\\" -> loops stackObj.Targets, gs.Battlefield.GetCard(target.CardID), sets Card.SkipNextUntap = true (consumed one-shot by Zone.UntapAll, same field Exert uses); shared by triggered/activated ability effects AND v2 spell-effect-sequence atoms (same chokepoint as \\\"tap