{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_5206ed2e-a306-4246-9ac9-26e962afbb2f","role":"user","created":1789883102,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"call_58f9e8a0ecc44030a98bf519","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"resultType":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","text":"func (gs *GameState) ExecuteAbilityEffect(stackObj *StackObject) error {\n\tif stackObj == nil || !stackObj.IsAbility {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\t// event_amount count spec (ticket #3730): the resolving object's own\n\t// stamped event magnitude (StackObject.EventAmount, set by\n\t// stampEventCard) is exposed to EvalDynamicAmountFull via a\n\t// GameState-scoped field for the duration of this call — the spec\n\t// resolves to the triggering event's numeric magnitude (\"put that\n\t// many\"). Saved/restored so nested effect execution (a sequence atom\n\t// resolving another ability) can't read a stale magnitude.\n\tsavedEventAmount := gs.eventAmountStamped\n\tif stackObj.HasEventAmount {\n\t\tgs.eventAmountStamped = stackObj.EventAmount\n\t} else {\n\t\tgs.eventAmountStamped = 0\n\t}\n\tdefer func() { gs.eventAmountStamped = savedEventAmount }()\n\n\teffect := stackObj.Text\n\tsource := stackObj.Card\n\teffectValue := stackObj.EffectValue\n\ttargets := stackObj.Targets\n\tif role, _ := effectValue[\"sequence_target_role\"].(string); role == \"referent\" {\n\t\tif len(targets) > 1 {\n\t\t\ttargets = targets[:1]\n\t\t}\n\t} else if role == \"recipient\" {\n\t\tif len(targets) > 1 {\n\t\t\ttargets = targets[1:]\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\ttargets = nil\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t// delayed_return_to_hand_next_end_step primitive (ticket\n\t// engine.auto-delayed-return-to-hand-at-next-end-step-b302082c07, Dragon\n\t// Mask class). Dispatches straight to executeReturnToHandDelayedEffect,\n\t// which arms the one-shot EventEndStep closure described there.\n\tif effect == \"delayed_return_to_hand_next_end_step\" {\n\t\treturn gs.executeReturnToHandDelayedEffect(targets)\n\t}\n\n\tif effect == \"destroy_up_to_counter_count\" {\n\t\treturn gs.executeDestroyUpToCounterCountTargets(source, targets, effectValue)\n\t}\n\t// mass_destroy_attack_relative_untapped_continuous_control_filter (Total\n\t// War class): connects ResolveTriggerReferentPlayerController (already\n\t// present, only unit-tested, never called from here) into the ability's\n\t// effective controller, so effectValue[\"controller_ref\"] ==\n\t// \"trigger_referent_player\" resolves to the triggering event's stamped\n\t// player (stackObj.EventPlayer, the ATTACKING player for an \"attacks\"\n\t// event with Controller:\"any\") instead of the ability's own controller.\n\t// A no-op for every other card: absent controller_ref returns\n\t// stackObj.Controller unchanged.\n\teventPlayer := -1\n\tif stackObj.HasEventPlayer {\n\t\teventPlayer = stackObj.EventPlayer\n\t}\n\tcontroller := gs.ResolveTriggerReferentPlayerController(effectValue, stackObj.Controller, eventPlayer)\n\tif ref, _ := effectValue[\"controller_ref\"].(string); ref == \"trigger_source_controller\" &&\n\t\tstackObj.EventCard != nil &&\n\t\tstackObj.EventCard.Controller >= 0 &&\n\t\tstackObj.EventCard.Controller < len(gs.Players) {\n\t\tcontroller = stackObj.EventCard.Controller\n\t}\n\n\t// destroy_all_matching_trigger_spell_mana_value implements Celestial\n\t// Kirin's dynamic referent: all permanents whose mana value equals the\n\t// triggering spell's mana value.\n\tif effect == \"destroy_all_matching_trigger_spell_mana_value\" {\n\t\tif stackObj.EventCard == nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}\n\t\tfilter := \"permanent_mv_eq_\" + strconv.Itoa(stackObj.EventCard.ManaCost.CMC())\n\t\treturn gs.destroyAllMatching(controller, filter, \"\", false, \"\", false, \"\")\n\t}\n\n\tif effect == \"exile_target_graveyard_card_and_named_matches\" {\n\t\treturn gs.executeExileTargetGraveyardCardAndNamedMatches(targets)\n\t}\n\n\t// targeted_graveyard_card_to_owner_library_bottom primitive (ticket\n\t// engine.auto-targeted-graveyard-card-to-owner-library-bottom--e51521cad3,\n\t// Reito Lantern class: \"Put target card from a graveyard on the bottom\n\t// of its owner's library.\"). The executor executeGraveyardCardToOwnerLibraryBottom\n\t// (defined above, ticket f6061a6cee) already implements the semantics --\n\t// any player's graveyard as the source zone, destination always the\n\t// targeted card's OWNER's library bottom -- but had no dispatch case, so\n\t// a parser-emitted effect never reached it. This is a pure connection:\n\t// hand the resolved controller and the chosen card targets straight to\n\t// the existing helper. The generic return_from_graveyard effect keeps its\n\t// own controller-graveyard/controller-library semantics untouched, and\n\t// untargeted cards in the selected graveyard are never moved.\n\tif effect == \"targeted_graveyard_card_to_owner_library_bottom\" {\n\t\treturn gs.executeGraveyardCardToOwnerLibraryBottom(controller, targets)\n\t}\n\n\t// self_exile_from_graveyard_with_dependent_trigger primitive (ticket","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"func (gs *GameState) ExecuteAbilityEffect(stackObj *StackObject) error {\n\tif stackObj == nil || !stackObj.IsAbility {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\t// event_amount count spec (ticket #3730): the resolving object's own\n\t// stamped event magnitude (StackObject.EventAmount, set by\n\t// stampEventCard) is exposed to EvalDynamicAmountFull via a\n\t// GameState-scoped field for the duration of this call — the spec\n\t// resolves to the triggering event's numeric magnitude (\"put that\n\t// many\"). Saved/restored so nested effect execution (a sequence atom\n\t// resolving another ability) can't read a stale magnitude.\n\tsavedEventAmount := gs.eventAmountStamped\n\tif stackObj.HasEventAmount {\n\t\tgs.eventAmountStamped = stackObj.EventAmount\n\t} else {\n\t\tgs.eventAmountStamped = 0\n\t}\n\tdefer func() { gs.eventAmountStamped = savedEventAmount }()\n\n\teffect := stackObj.Text\n\tsource := stackObj.Card\n\teffectValue := stackOb